        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'They're putting up quite a fight': Hezbollah pushes back against Israel's advancing troops Middle East Issued on: 27/03/2026 - 07:58 FRANCE 24 correspondent Renée Davis reports from Beirut, where Israel on Friday carried out fresh air strikes on the once densely packed southern suburbs. And in the country's south, Shiite group Hezbollah said its fighters continued to push back against Israel's ground offensive. 'Justice necessary': Yazidi survivors deliver harrowing genocide testimony amid int'l indifference 27/03/2026 Middle East Trump again berates NATO for inaction in securing Strait of Hormuz 26/03/2026 Middle East Trump insists Iran is ‘begging to make a deal’ after Tehran dismisses ceasefire plan 26/03/2026 Middle East As 'war of choice' escalates into international crisis, Miller says Trump has 'no strategy' 26/03/2026 Middle East 'Tehran assumes war is behind them: Iran will not capitulate, Trump has it all wrong' 26/03/2026 Middle East US claims 'strong signs' for deal with Iran 26/03/2026 Middle East Oil, stock trading spikes before Trump's Iran remarks spark insider trading suspicions 25/03/2026 Middle East Georgia’s links to Iran: Ex-Defense Minister Khidasheli denounces Al-Mustafa University activities 25/03/2026 Europe 'Difficult to overemphasise how risky it would be for the US' to put boots on the ground: expert 25/03/2026 Middle East"
